# API documentation (required)

Read `AGENTS.md` for full instructions.

## Architecture
- **Separate client & server** — deploy independently, no `shared/` folder
- **Separate env:** `client/.env` and `server/.env.local` only
- **No `apps/` folder** — use root `client/` and `server/`
- **No root node_modules**

## Client UI
- Reuse existing components (Button, FormModal, Table, Tabs, PageHeader, PasswordInput, etc.) — do not duplicate or move them
- **New** component placement: primitives → `components/ui/primitives/`; forms → `components/ui/forms/`; navigation → `components/ui/navigation/`; layout → `components/layout/`; features → `features/<feature>/components/`; routes → `routes/`
- **Existing** screens stay in `pages/<feature>/`; new features use `features/<feature>/`; keep entry files thin
- New pages layout: `PageContainer` + `PageHeader` + `Table` / `Tabs` + `FormModal` (match `employees/EmployeesPage`, `registrations/RegistrationsPage`)
- Tables: center-aligned by default; use `Table` `align` prop or per-column `align` — never hardcode `text-left`/`text-right` on columns for alignment
- Form inputs: pass `icon` on every `Input` / `PasswordInput` / `Select` / `Textarea` — all existing and new forms (see `login/LoginForm`, `register/RegisterForm`, `employees/CreateEmployeeModal`)
- Create forms: save disabled until required fields filled; edit forms: save disabled until data changes
- PATCH only changed fields; server applies partial updates
- Password fields use `PasswordInput`; buttons show spinner while loading; use colorful `react-icons`

## Code style
- Use **arrow functions** everywhere in `client/src/` and `server/src/` — no `function` declarations (see `AGENTS.md` → Code style)

## Node.js
- Minimum **Node 22+**

## Types and utils
- Duplicate types/utils in each app (no shared imports)

## Every API endpoint
Update **both** in the same PR (no markdown API docs):
1. `docs/openapi.yaml` — path, schemas, auth, examples
2. `docs/postman/hr-saas.postman_collection.json` — runnable request; save `accessToken` in test script when returned

## README
Update `README.md` when setup, env, commands, architecture, or deployment changes. Link to `docs/openapi.yaml` and `docs/postman/` for API details — do not duplicate them.
